    "cultural_notes_vi": "Korean critical essay opening conventions: (1) Korean academic 비평 traditionally open formally — author + work overview. Modern 비평 (post-1960s 김현 era) introduces more inventive openings; (2) Three opening styles dominant in contemporary Korean literary criticism: (a) 화두 던지기 (throwing keynote concept), (b) 일화 도입 (anecdote), (c) 문제 제기 (problem statement); (3) 김현 famous for short, incisive openings — often single sentence 'X란 ~다' definition challenge; (4) 신형철 known for personal-essay-style openings borrowing creative writing tradition; (5) 학회 발표 (academic conference) papers often more formal opening — title + author + research question; literary 평론 (review essays in 「문학동네」, 「창작과비평」) more flexible; (6) Length conventions: short essay (1500-2000자) = opening 10-15%; long essay (5000자+) = opening 5-10%; (7) Vietnamese learner: opening conventions differ across Korean contexts — academic vs literary essay. Confirm target venue before drafting opening; (8) Korean critical culture appreciates 명문 (well-crafted prose) — opening sentence often anthologized, quoted, taught. 김현의 첫 문장 famous in Korean criticism circles.",
    "tip_advice_vi": "Opening writing 5-step: (1) DEFINE function — what should opening accomplish (capture attention + signal approach + introduce text)?; (2) AVOID announcement — '이 글은 ~을 다룬다' (this piece deals with ~) is amateur; instead, perform the analysis; (3) CHOOSE strategy — concept-shaking, anecdote, problem statement, image, quotation, provocation; (4) WRITE shortest possible — opening should be efficient, no padding; (5) VERIFY tone match — opening tone must align with body tone. C2 best practices: (a) Don't summarize work in opening — analyze instead; (b) Don't biographize author in opening unless critical to argument; (c) Don't reveal thesis in opening — 'predict-the-conclusion' opening kills suspense; (d) DO foreshadow critical move — let reader know what kind of analysis is coming. Try writing opening LAST — after body is drafted, opening is easier because you know what you're opening into. Sai lầm thường gặp: (a) Cliché opening — 'in our globalized age', 'X is one of the most important writers'; (b) Throat-clearing — 'in this essay I will examine'; (c) Over-quotation — letting epigraph do all work; (d) Personal anecdote that doesn't connect to critical argument.",
